<title>SWEDEN: Riksbank board meeting ends, no rate changes.</title>
<headline>Riksbank board meeting ends, no rate changes.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, ended a board meeting on Thursday with no changes announced to interest rates.</p>
<p>The market had not expected the Riksbank to make any moves.</p>
<p>The bank's key interest rate, the repo, currently stands at 4.10 percent. It was last lowered on December 17.</p>
<p>Its other key rates, the deposit and lending rates, stand at 3.75 percent and 5.25 percent respectively.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
